---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArchitectureLayers from '../components/ArchitectureLayers.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Architecture — Vericore" description="Understand the Vericore 0.7.0 deterministic analysis, context, Engineering Reality, evidence, governance, planning, and verification architecture.">
  <section class="hero container"><span class="kicker">VERICORE 0.7.0 / ARCHITECTURE</span><h1>Evidence flows<br /><span>through the system.</span></h1><p>Vericore separates deterministic repository facts from higher-level reasoning and delivery surfaces so engineering outputs remain traceable to evidence and repository state.</p></section>
  <section class="container pipeline" aria-label="Vericore architecture flow">
    <div class="node primary"><small>INPUT</small><strong>Repository + Git</strong><span>Java/Kotlin source · history · working-tree state</span></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="node"><small>ANALYSIS</small><strong>Scanner + parsers + Git intelligence</strong><span>Structure · dependencies · cycles · PageRank · churn · authorship · evolution · reports</span></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="node"><small>ARTIFACT</small><strong>Analysis Snapshot + Engineering Context</strong><span>Versioned signals, repository-relative fingerprints, stable digests, context snapshots and diffs</span></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="node reality"><small>REALITY</small><strong>Engineering Reality</strong><span>Deterministic identity binding analysis and repository context; stale analysis can be rejected</span></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="node evidence"><small>GROUNDING</small><strong>Evidence + deterministic intelligence</strong><span>Impact · PR · architecture · drift · Q&amp;A retrieval · test signals · planning inputs · provenance</span></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="outputs"><div class="node"><small>OUTPUT</small><strong>Repository Q&amp;A</strong><span>Intent classification, bounded evidence, deterministic ranking, optional AI</span></div><div class="node"><small>OUTPUT</small><strong>Engineering Planner</strong><span>Read-only implementation and verification plan from grounded evidence</span></div><div class="node"><small>GOVERNANCE</small><strong>Architecture Contracts</strong><span>Explicit baseline, limits, deterministic decisions and idempotent records</span></div></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="node verify"><small>SAFETY</small><strong>Prepare → Change → Verify</strong><span>Persist Agent Change Contract before implementation; verify the original artifact afterwards</span></div><div class="arrow">↓</div>
    <div class="node"><small>DELIVERY</small><strong>CLI · REST · MCP · CI · HTML</strong><span>Local workflows, trusted agent integration, automated verification, self-contained reports</span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="container split"><article><span class="kicker">01 / DETERMINISTIC</span><h2>Repository facts</h2><p>Source structure, dependencies, Git signals, architecture findings, and history are established before optional model reasoning.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">02 / STATE</span><h2>Engineering Reality</h2><p>Analysis and repository context receive a deterministic identity. Wall-clock timestamps do not silently make equivalent state look different.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">03 / GOVERNANCE</span><h2>Architecture contracts</h2><p>Explicit baselines can be evaluated against findings, cycles, and layer limits with stable decision records.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">04 / SAFETY</span><h2>Persisted change boundary</h2><p>The Agent Change Contract binds planned paths, evidence, verification commands, architecture expectations, and repository identity. Verify checks the persisted contract rather than regenerating it.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">05 / AI</span><h2>Reasoning is downstream</h2><p>AI is disabled unless configured. When invoked, providers receive bounded repository-derived context instead of being treated as the source of repository truth.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">06 / DELIVERY</span><h2>Local interfaces</h2><p>The CLI is the primary workflow surface; REST and MCP expose local/internal integrations. Neither is an authentication or tenant-isolation layer.</p></article></section>
  <section class="container"><ArchitectureLayers /></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.hero{padding:110px 0 70px;max-width:920px}.kicker{color:var(--accent);font:600 .72rem/1.2 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em}.hero h1{margin:18px 0;font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,6rem);line-height:.96;letter-spacing:-.065em}.hero h1 span{color:var(--muted)}.hero p{max-width:760px;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.15rem}.pipeline{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center}.node{width:min(780px,100%);padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--panel);display:grid;gap:6px}.node.primary{border-color:#31536a;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0e1922,var(--panel))}.node.reality{border-color:#4b5563}.node.evidence,.node.verify{border-color:#365f52}.node small{color:var(--muted);font:.68rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.1em}.node strong{font-size:1.1rem}.node span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.86rem}.arrow{padding:8px 0;color:var(--accent);font:1.3rem ui-monospace,monospace}.outputs{width:min(1000px,100%);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px}.outputs .node{width:auto}.split{margin-top:90px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:12px}.split article{padding:30px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--panel)}.split h2{margin:12px 0 8px;font-size:1.6rem}.split p{color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:900px){.outputs,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.outputs .node:last-child,.split article:last-child{grid-column:1/-1}}@media(max-width:700px){.outputs,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr}.outputs .node:last-child,.split article:last-child{grid-column:auto}}
</style>
